      "verification": "not_recorded",
      "verification_note": "The 2024 Individual Income Tax Statistical Report (https://revenue.iowa.gov/media/4509/download?inline=, sha256 6ce7019f1f7d2b46be4c9bdcad3dcd3fba2e720ecdeb3fb061c8a7073581c306, retrieved 2026-11-10) Table 1 states 4.40% over $0 but not over $6,210, 4.82% over $6,210 but not over $31,050, and 5.70% over $31,050, and a single 3.8% rate for 2025. It does not print the held joint edges $12,420 and $62,100. The 2024 expanded instructions (https://revenue.iowa.gov/media/4152/download?inline=, sha256 7257943544f063e3a3ec0832ade29127f23f48090da90b9b34cc1e327dc3b8cd, retrieved 2026-11-10) state the 3.8% rate for 2025 and say to enter the standard deduction reported on federal Form 1040, line 12. They do not print the 2024 brackets. https://revenue.iowa.gov/press-release/2023-10-25/idr-announces-2024-individual-income-tax-brackets-and-interest-rates returned HTTP 403 on 2026-11-10.",
